  "body": "## Issue\nCloses #995\nClaim: cloud/i995-opus\nAuthor model: Opus 5.5 (cloud/i995-opus)\nReviewer model: Fable 5.2 (swifthfr.cloud-i995-opus.adversarial-reviewer.pr996, round 1: swifthfr.cloud-i995-opus.adversarial-reviewer.pr996-r1)\n\n## What and why\n\n**Problem.** Since 2026-11-17 00:20 UTC, `ReaderPageEndWebTests` (`atRestTheHintSitsTheSharedGapUnderTheLastMessageAboveTheBar`, `aTallPageReportsItsEndOnlyWhenItIsScrolledThere`) and `ReaderInsetsWebTests` (`aRefreshReopensAtTheSameMessageWhenTheBarsChanged`, and `aRefreshAfterAPinchZoomReopensAtTheSameMessage` in job 133770412196) fail now and then on the iOS 27 simulator.\n\n**Cause (one signal for all three).** The tests treat `ready` as \"the scroll view shows the document\". `ready` is posted by `reader.js` from the WebContent process; the UI process applies the document's first layer-tree commit (content size + WebKit's reset to the top, see `WebKitResetWatch`) later. Under load the gap is wide enough to be seen.\n\n| Test | What it waited on | Why not deterministic | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `atRestTheHint…` | `ready`, then \"offset within 2 of `contentSize + 50 − bounds`\" | Before the commit `contentSize` is the blank page's (650 = 800 − 100 − 50): the \"end\" is −100, the offset already there, so the wait passes on its first poll and the hint is measured with the page at its top | jobs 133712438518, 133717388761, 133753519977, 133769701618, 133770412196: band `0.0...650.0` (offset −100), hint at 3070–3101, test over in 1–3 s |\n| `aTallPage…` | same, then a way back to `last() − 20` | Same stale `last()` = −100: target −120, unreachable, 60 s timeout | job 133712438518: `offset (0.0, -100.0), target -120.0` |\n| `aRefreshReopens…` / `aRefreshAfterAPinchZoom…` | the new page's `scrollY` = 1000 | Before WebKit's reset the scroll view still shows the old document at the same reading top (offset 900 under 100 = 1000): the new page's `scrollY` can read 1000 before the reset puts it back to 0 and the held restore runs. Likely cause, read from the code: the log shows `scrollY` 0 right after `settled`, while the later offset-900 and `readingTop` checks of the same 1 s test passed (so the app's restore did land) | jobs 133772120017, 133770412196 |\n\n**#943.** Its stylesheet changes only CSS values (margins, font sizes, quote fill); nothing in it changes when `ready` is sent or when WebKit commits. It is not shown to be the trigger; runner load (`Timed out waiting for Launch Services database update`, WebContent launches over 1 s in the same windows) widens the existing gap.\n\n**Change (tests only, no app code).**\n- `showsDocument(_:)` (`ReaderWebTestSupport`): waits until the scroll view's content height (at zoom 1) is within 2 points of the page's `scrollHeight` (the agreement green end-of-page runs show; blank page 650 vs documents of 3000+). The new document's size only reaches the scroll view through a layer-tree commit after the navigation's commit, the same one that applies WebKit's reset. Only valid for a page taller than the viewport (stated in its comment; all callers are).\n- Page-end tests: `showsDocument` after `ready`, before any scroll and before `last()` is computed.\n- Insets tests: `showsDocument` before the first document's own scroll, in the three tests that scroll it (same class, no failure seen there yet). The refresh restore waits on `restored(_:token:in:timeout:)`: the reset watch committed the new document and has ended (the reset came, the restore was sent), **and** the page's `scrollY` and the scroll view's `readingTop` both equal the target. The post-load assertions (`scrollY after load`, offset 900, `readingTop`) are unchanged.\n\nWhy this wide: these are the only tests that scroll a freshly loaded page themselves or read a restore from the page side; the landing test (`ReaderWebControllerTests`) goes through the app's landing, which already waits for the reset.\n\n## Review\n- Round 0 (head d03c371): APPROVED, 1 medium (not run yet), 1 low (tolerance 1 → 2), 2 details (comments). Verdict posted verbatim.\n- Round 1 (head cb55d4b): low and details fixed; APPROVED. Remaining medium: the 20-run proof before merge.\n\n## How it was verified\n- App tests cannot run on Linux: `compile-check` label for the macOS build; SwiftLint clean locally on the three files.\n- No assertion loosened, no skip, no sleep-only wait.\n- **Open:** 20 runs of each test on the CI simulator or the Mac (`host: mac-helps`) before merge; #995 is not to be closed on the review alone.\n\n## Checklist (AGENTS.md §9)\n- [x] Module boundaries respected\n- [x] Tests updated (synchronisation only)\n- [x] No secrets; fixtures anonymized\n- [x] Docs updated: none needed (test-only)\n- [x] Author model: Opus 5.5 / Reviewer model: Fable 5.2 (must differ)\n- [x] No legacy behaviour changed: no `### Ledger` section\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_014QH2CJP7xdb4wGyXAmFjPW",
