   "body": "Agent: swifthfr.cloud-i995-opus.adversarial-reviewer.pr996 (Fable 5.2)\n\n**Adversarial review (Fable 5.2): APPROVED** — head d03c371840c284d90d2bee4df7fe8ef08539bcfe\n\nNo assertion loosened, no test skipped, no sleep-only fix. Both new waits are bounded and cannot pass on stale state.\n\n1. **Medium — the fix has never run.** The head's \"App build + tests\" job (133791800434) failed at the draft gate in 2 s, and the compile check was still in progress. Mark ready and get the simulator job green, ideally twice, before merge: the hint test failed in 5 of 6 jobs, so a green run is real evidence.\n2. **Low — `ReaderWebTestSupport.swift:129`**: `showsDocument` needs `contentSize.height` within 1 point of `scrollHeight`. Existing green runs only prove 2 (`abs(offset - last()) <= 2`). If the gap exceeds 1, five tests fail after 240 s each. Use 2, or confirm on the first run.\n3. **Detail — `ReaderInsetsWebTests.swift:115`**: \"the offset was right 30 s later\" is wrong. Job 133772120017 ran the whole test in 1.053 s; the offset wait passed inside its 30 s deadline.\n4. **Detail — `ReaderInsetsWebTests.swift:139,157,201`**: no CI failure is attributed to these three `showsDocument` calls; the failures were at the refresh (lines 161 and 192). Harmless, but the comment gives a cause no log shows.\n\nRoot causes:\n- **Page-end tests**: proven by the logs. Target -120 and band 0...650 both mean a content height of 650 with a tall page.\n- **Refresh tests**: marked \"likely\", which is honest. In job 133772120017 the later offset checks passed, so the restore was not lost and the old wait read a transient.\n- **App race**: none masked. `restored` requires the reset seen (`committedToken == token`, `token == nil`) and both sides at the target, so a restore lost for good still times out.\n\n**Verified**: diff identical to `origin/dev-swift...HEAD` (3 test files); SwiftLint clean on them; the 6 failure logs read against `WebKitResetWatch.swift`, `ReaderWebController.swift` and `reader.js`; job ids in the comments match the logs. Not run: build and tests (no Xcode on Linux), so no red-without-the-change proof beyond the CI logs.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
