   "body": "Agent : swifthfr.cloud-i995-opus.adversarial-reviewer.pr996-r1 (Fable 5.2)\n\n**Adversarial review (Fable 5.2): APPROVED** — head cb55d4bffb08200314bfa5516d917d1f5f9aa760\n\nRound-1 findings:\n- (2) Handled. `showsDocument` now waits within 2 points (`ReaderWebTestSupport.swift:130`), the bound the green end-of-page checks support (`ReaderPageEndWebTests.swift:55,80`). Not a loosened assertion: the helper is new in this PR, it is a precondition wait, the states it separates differ by thousands of points (blank 650 vs 3000+), and every assertion after it is unchanged.\n- (3) Handled. `ReaderInsetsWebTests.swift:115-117` now matches job 133772120017 (one issue, 1.053 s) and says the cause is read from the code.\n- (4) Handled. The three first-document comments (`:140`, `:159`, `:204`) say \"would be\", \"no failure seen here yet\".\n\nNew findings:\n1. **Medium — nothing in this PR has been executed.** The PR is a draft, so \"App build + tests\" stops at the draft gate on both commits (job 133793386810), and the compile check was still running. Issue #995's third criterion (each test green 20 times on the CI simulator) is open. Risk: the three new `showsDocument` preconditions in `ReaderInsetsWebTests` have never been seen to hold for `tallDocument`; if content size and `scrollHeight` differ by more than 2 there, each test fails after 240 s. Fix: do the 20 runs before merge; do not close #995 on this approval.\n2. **Detail** — `ReaderWebTestSupport.swift:123-124`: the 2-point agreement is inferred from the end-of-page offset check, not measured directly; no log prints `contentSize` beside `scrollHeight`.\n\nNo sleep-only wait, no skip, no assertion loosened: the refresh wait is stricter (reset seen for token 2, then page and scroll view both at the reading top).\n\n**Verified**: full diff and round-1 diff read against `WebKitResetWatch.swift` and `ReaderWebController.swift`; comments checked against the six failure logs; SwiftLint on the three files: 0 violations; check runs of both commits read. Not run: the tests and the L01 revert probe (no Xcode on Linux).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
